# supercronic crontab for the depas-cron sidecar (TZ=America/Santiago).
#
# The pass is four stages, each on its own schedule. Run as separate entries they
# stop waiting on each other: a slow scrape no longer holds back an alert for a
# listing that was enriched an hour ago, and the enrichment gets 6 goes an hour
# instead of one, which clears a backlog six times faster without asking any portal
# for more requests per second. `depas watch` still runs all four in order if you
# would rather have one entry.
#
# Offset minutes rather than :00 so no portal sees a clock-aligned request, and
# staggered so the stages tend to run in the order they feed each other.

# Discovery: sweep DEPAS_COMMUNES on all six portals at once, then delist whatever
# no believable sweep has turned up. This is the one that must not stall.
#
# Three times an hour rather than one. It was the largest wait in the chain by far — a
# listing published at :08 waited until :07 the next hour to be seen at all — and the
# cutoff at DEPAS_SWEEP_QUIET_PAGES makes an incremental sweep cheap: a portal with
# nothing new stops after two pages. It is still the only stage that costs the portals
# real requests, which is why it goes to three and not to twelve.
#
# DEPAS_DELIST_AFTER moves with this. It counts believable sweeps, not hours, so
# tripling the sweeps would have tripled how fast a listing is given up on — three
# sweeps used to be three hours of patience and would have become one. Its default went
# from 3 to 9 to keep the same wall clock.
7,27,47 * * * * depas discover

# Detail pages: the new ones first, then the re-reads. Every ten minutes, in small
# batches, which spreads the requests instead of firing 60 at the top of the hour.
2,12,22,32,42,52 * * * * depas enrich

# Travel times and the zone benchmarks. Transitous is somebody else's server, so this
# stays sequential and modest — but twice an hour meant a listing with nothing left to
# wait for but its travel time waited up to thirty minutes for it, which was the second
# biggest delay in the chain after discovery.
6,21,36,51 * * * * depas route

# Alerts, the corrections to cards already posted, and the pinned ⭐ list. Every five
# minutes: a pass with nothing to post asks Telegram nothing at all, so frequency here
# is free, and it is frequency rather than batch size that decides how long a listing
# waits — the batch only decides how fast a backlog drains.
*/5 * * * * depas announce

# Watchdog: warn the admins by DM about any stage that has stopped completing. Each
# stage stamps its own heartbeat, so a stalled enrichment is no longer hidden behind
# a scrape that keeps succeeding.
0 */4 * * * depas healthcheck
